                                <div id="padACEmpty" style="color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080);font-size:12px;font-family:monospace;">No PAD AC data saved for this job yet.</div>

                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- ================= ANTI-COLLISION PLOTS ================= -->
                <div class="accordion mb-2" id="accordionAcPlots">
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h2 class="accordion-header">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button"
                                    data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseAcPlots"
                                    aria-expanded="false">
                                📉 Anti-collision Plots
                            </button>
                        </h2>
                        <div id="collapseAcPlots" class="accordion-collapse collapse">
                            <div class="accordion-body p-2">
                                <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mb-2 flex-wrap">
                                    <label style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);">Reference Well:</label>
                                    <select id="acpRefSelect" class="form-select form-select-sm" style="max-width:280px;"></select>
                                    <button id="acpResetZoomBtn" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-info">⤢ Reset Zoom</button>
                                    <div class="form-check form-check-inline ms-2">
                                        <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="acpShowLegend">
                                        <label class="form-check-label" for="acpShowLegend" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);">Show Legend</label>
                                    </div>
                                    <!-- ADDED 2026-10-11: color scheme. Standard = Subjects blue, Offsets red, iPlan scenarios green dotted.
                                         Multi-Color = previous behavior (one palette color per wellbore; scenarios still green dotted). -->
                                    <label style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);">Colors:</label>
                                    <select id="acpColorMode" class="form-select form-select-sm" style="max-width:130px;">
                                        <option value="standard" selected>Standard</option>
                                        <option value="multi">Multi-Color</option>
                                    </select>
                                    <label style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);">Toolcode:</label>
                                    <select id="acpToolcode" class="form-select form-select-sm" style="max-width:220px;">
                                        <option value="">— Simplified (approximate) —</option>
                                    </select>
                                    <label style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);" title="sigma_sep multiplier for SF = dist / (K * sigma_sep). Default 2 = flat sigma multiplier, matching Compass's documented default report convention (its .xls AC reports state 'Output errors are at 2.00 sigma'). The dimensionally-correct 3-DOF chi-square 95% value would be 2.7955 instead - use that if reconciling against a report/policy that specifies a true multi-DOF confidence level rather than a flat sigma multiple. Adjust freely to match whatever confidence convention another tool's report used.">Confidence K (sigma):</label>
                                    <input type="number" id="acpKSF" step="0.001" min="0.01" value="2" class="form-control form-control-sm" style="max-width:90px;">
                                    <label style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);" title="Evaluate C2C/SF at a specific reference-well MD against every offset well, e.g. to cross-check a specific row from another program's report — interpolated between the reference well's own survey stations, not snapped to the nearest one.">Evaluate at Ref MD:</label>
                                    <input type="number" id="acpEvalMd" step="0.01" placeholder="e.g. 775" class="form-control form-control-sm" style="max-width:100px;">
                                    <button id="acpEvalMdBtn" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-info">Evaluate</button>
                                    <span id="acpStatus" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080);font-family:monospace;"></span>
                                </div>
                                <div id="acpEvalMdPanel" style="display:none;font-size:11px;font-family:monospace;background:var(--an-panel2,#161e28);border:1px solid #39ff14;border-radius:4px;padding:8px 10px;margin-bottom:8px;"></div>
                                <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mb-2 flex-wrap" style="border-top:1px dashed #2a3a4a;padding-top:8px;">
                                    <label style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);" title="Upload a Compass 'Error Ellipse Survey' PDF report for the current reference well. Extracts MD/Inc/Az/Semi-major/Semi-minor per station and lines it up next to MTX's own computed ellipse at the same stations, so the two can be checked row by row. STATUS 2026-08-21: the MWD+HRGM toolcode was found to be missing its SAG and XYM3/XYM4 systematic misalignment terms (both confirmed against Compass's own .ipm export and added to iscwsaToolcodes.json) — this closed the Semi-major/Semi-minor gap from ~2x low to within ~2-9%, confirmed against this well's own report. Only checked for MWD+HRGM; other toolcodes' .ipm files haven't been checked for the same gap.">Upload Error Ellipse (Compass PDF):</label>
                                    <input type="file" id="acpErrEllipseFile" accept=".pdf" class="form-control form-control-sm" style="max-width:260px;">
                                    <span id="acpErrEllipseStatus" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080);font-family:monospace;"></span>
                                </div>
                                <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mb-2 flex-wrap">
                                    <label style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);" title="Which offset well the Center-to-Centre / Separation Factor columns below are computed against — must match the offset well the uploaded Anticollision PDF's section is for.">Offset Well (for C2C/SF):</label>
                                    <select id="acpErrEllipseOffsetWell" class="form-select form-select-sm" style="max-width:220px;"></select>
                                    <label style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);" title="Upload a Compass 'Anticollision' PDF report (the one with the per-offset-well Reference/Offset MD, Semi Major Axis, Between Centres, Between Ellipses, Minimum Separation, Separation Factor table). Only the section for the offset well selected above is used — matched by its 'Offset Design: ...' header. C2C/SF rows are matched to Error Ellipse rows by nearest reference-well MD.">Upload Anticollision (Compass PDF):</label>
                                    <input type="file" id="acpAntiCollFile" accept=".pdf" class="form-control form-control-sm" style="max-width:260px;">
                                    <span id="acpAntiCollStatus" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080);font-family:monospace;"></span>
                                </div>
                                <div id="acpErrEllipsePanel" style="display:none;font-size:11px;font-family:monospace;background:var(--an-panel2,#161e28);border:1px solid #ffb020;border-radius:4px;padding:8px 10px;margin-bottom:8px;max-height:420px;overflow:auto;"></div>
                                <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mb-2 flex-wrap" style="border-top:1px dashed #2a3a4a;padding-top:8px;">
                                    <button id="acpMtxAcReportBtn" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-warning" title="Builds an MTX-computed anticollision report, station-by-station for the selected Reference Well, against every offset well currently plotted — same layout as Compass's own 'Anticollision with Risk' report. All values come from MTX's own ISCWSA engine (same functions already used/validated above by the Evaluate-at-MD and Error Ellipse comparison panels), not from an uploaded Compass file.">📋 Build MTX AC Report</button>
                                    <span id="acpMtxAcReportStatus" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080);font-family:monospace;"></span>
                                    <button id="acpMtxAcReportXlsBtn" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-success" style="display:none;">⬇ Download Excel</button>
                                </div>
                                <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mb-2 flex-wrap" style="border-top:1px dashed #2a3a4a;padding-top:8px;">
                                    <label style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);" title="The physical borehole/casing radius sum (Rref+Roff, i.e. what the SPE-184644 slides call R1=Ro+Rr) that defines a 'direct hit' — a sample landing within this distance of the reference well's centerline counts as a hit. MTX does not model per-well borehole/casing radius (TBR) anywhere else in this tool, so there is nothing to default this to; you must supply it (e.g. sum of each well's own hole/casing OD/2, converted to metres). Leaving it at 0 makes 'hit' mean literal centerline-to-centerline crossing, which is the most conservative (smallest) possible hit volume, not a realistic borehole intersection.">Combined Hit Radius Rref+Roff (m):</label>
                                    <input type="number" id="acpHitRadius" step="0.001" min="0" value="0.17" placeholder="e.g. 0.31 for two 12-1/4in holes" class="form-control form-control-sm" style="max-width:220px;">
                                    <label style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);" title="Number of Monte Carlo trials per row/station. Higher = less sampling noise but slower (trials × rows total samples). 2500 is the person's own requested default (2026-08-22).">MC Trials:</label>
                                    <input type="number" id="acpMcTrials" step="1" min="10" value="2500" class="form-control form-control-sm" style="max-width:90px;">
                                    <button id="acpMcPocBtn" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-danger" title="Monte Carlo estimate of Probability of Collision (Direct Hit): for every row of the already-built MTX AC Report, samples the RAW (unscaled, no Confidence-K) combined relative-position uncertainty — Σcomb = Σref + Σoff, the ISCWSA covariance already computed for this pair, summed with no cross-well correlation (the 'independent, most common assumption' case per Jon Bang SPE-184644 slide 24, same default already used for Separation Factor elsewhere in this tool) — as a 3D Gaussian centred on the actual relative position vector, and counts what fraction of samples land within the Combined Hit Radius of the reference centerline. This directly evaluates the same 'probability = integral of pdf over specific volume' definition given in SPE-184644 (slides 5/15) and the person's own notes, via numerical Monte Carlo integration instead of a closed-form formula — no drilling-engineering formula is invented here, only generic Gaussian sampling of the already-validated ISCWSA covariance. Build the report first.">🎲 Run Monte Carlo POC</button>
                                </div>
                                <div id="acpMtxAcReportPanel" style="display:none;font-size:11px;font-family:monospace;background:var(--an-panel2,#161e28);border:1px solid #79c0ff;border-radius:4px;padding:8px 10px;margin-bottom:8px;max-height:520px;overflow:auto;"></div>
                                <div id="acpEmpty" style="color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080);font-size:12px;font-family:monospace;padding:8px;display:none;">
                                    Need at least 2 wellbores with survey data loaded in the 3D viewer above.
                                </div>
                                <div id="acpMagCards" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(190px,1fr));gap:6px;margin-bottom:8px;"></div>
                                <div id="acpDataWarnings" style="margin-bottom:6px;"></div>
                                <div id="acpChartWrap" style="display:none;gap:8px;">
                                    <div id="acpChartC2CWrap" style="flex:1;min-width:0;height:460px;background:var(--an-panel2,#161e28);border:1px solid var(--an-border);border-radius:4px;padding:8px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;">
                                        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-size:10px;color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080);margin-bottom:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
                                            <span>X:</span>
                                            <input type="number" id="acpC2cXMin" placeholder="0" style="width:60px;background:var(--an-panel,#111820);border:1px solid var(--an-border);color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);border-radius:3px;padding:2px 4px;font-size:10px;">
                                            <span>to</span>
                                            <input type="number" id="acpC2cXMax" placeholder="auto" style="width:60px;background:var(--an-panel,#111820);border:1px solid var(--an-border);color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);border-radius:3px;padding:2px 4px;font-size:10px;">
                                            <span style="margin-left:10px;">Y:</span>
                                            <input type="number" id="acpC2cYMin" placeholder="0" style="width:50px;background:var(--an-panel,#111820);border:1px solid var(--an-border);color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);border-radius:3px;padding:2px 4px;font-size:10px;">
                                            <span>to</span>
                                            <input type="number" id="acpC2cYMax" placeholder="20" style="width:50px;background:var(--an-panel,#111820);border:1px solid var(--an-border);color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);border-radius:3px;padding:2px 4px;font-size:10px;">
                                        </div>
