                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div id="acpChartSFWrap" style="flex:1;min-width:0;height:460px;background:var(--an-panel2,#161e28);border:1px solid var(--an-border);border-radius:4px;padding:8px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;">
                                        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-size:10px;color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080);margin-bottom:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
                                            <span>X:</span>
                                            <input type="number" id="acpSfXMin" placeholder="0" style="width:60px;background:var(--an-panel,#111820);border:1px solid var(--an-border);color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);border-radius:3px;padding:2px 4px;font-size:10px;">
                                            <span>to</span>
                                            <input type="number" id="acpSfXMax" placeholder="auto" style="width:60px;background:var(--an-panel,#111820);border:1px solid var(--an-border);color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);border-radius:3px;padding:2px 4px;font-size:10px;">
                                            <span style="margin-left:10px;">Y:</span>
                                            <input type="number" id="acpSfYMin" placeholder="0" style="width:50px;background:var(--an-panel,#111820);border:1px solid var(--an-border);color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);border-radius:3px;padding:2px 4px;font-size:10px;">
                                            <span>to</span>
                                            <input type="number" id="acpSfYMax" placeholder="2" style="width:50px;background:var(--an-panel,#111820);border:1px solid var(--an-border);color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);border-radius:3px;padding:2px 4px;font-size:10px;">
                                        </div>
                                        <div style="flex:1;min-height:0;position:relative;">
                                            <canvas id="acpChartSF"></canvas>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div id="acpDetailPanel" style="display:none;font-size:11px;font-family:monospace;background:var(--an-panel2,#161e28);border:1px solid #00c8ff;border-radius:4px;padding:8px 10px;margin-top:8px;"></div>

                                <!-- ================= TRAVELING CYLINDER PLOT ================= -->
                                <div style="margin-top:14px;border-top:1px solid var(--an-border);padding-top:10px;">
                                    <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mb-2 flex-wrap">
                                        <span style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--an-text-bright,#e8f4ff);">Traveling Cylinder Plot</span>
                                        <label style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);margin-left:8px;">Reference MD (m):</label>
                                        <input type="number" id="acpTcvRefMd" step="1" style="width:100px;background:var(--an-panel,#111820);border:1px solid var(--an-border);color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);border-radius:3px;padding:2px 6px;font-size:11px;">
                                        <label style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);margin-left:8px;">Window (± m):</label>
                                        <input type="number" id="acpTcvWindow" step="10" min="1" value="500" style="width:80px;background:var(--an-panel,#111820);border:1px solid var(--an-border);color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);border-radius:3px;padding:2px 6px;font-size:11px;">
                                        <label style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);margin-left:8px;">MD Interval (m):</label>
                                        <input type="number" id="acpTcvInterval" step="1" min="1" value="60" style="width:70px;background:var(--an-panel,#111820);border:1px solid var(--an-border);color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);border-radius:3px;padding:2px 6px;font-size:11px;">
                                        <label style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);margin-left:8px;">Max Scan Radius (m):</label>
                                        <input type="number" id="acpTcvMaxRadius" step="10" min="1" value="100" style="width:80px;background:var(--an-panel,#111820);border:1px solid var(--an-border);color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);border-radius:3px;padding:2px 6px;font-size:11px;">
                                        <div class="form-check form-check-inline ms-2">
                                            <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="acpTcvShowLabels">
                                            <label class="form-check-label" for="acpTcvShowLabels" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--an-text,#c8d8e8);">Show Depths</label>
                                        </div>
                                        <button id="acpTcvResetMdBtn" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-info">⤢ Reset to Deepest Station</button>
                                    </div>
                                    <div style="font-size:9px;color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080);margin-bottom:6px;">Scroll to zoom on the plot (stays centered on the reference well) — Max Scan Radius controls which crossings are computed at all, independent of the current zoom level. Drag the depth slider (or scroll over it) to travel down the reference well.</div>
                                    <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;max-width:620px;margin:0 auto;height:520px;">
                                        <div id="acpTcvSliderWrap" style="width:44px;flex-shrink:0;position:relative;background:var(--an-panel2,#161e28);border:1px solid var(--an-border);border-radius:4px;">
                                            <div id="acpTcvSliderTrack" style="position:absolute;left:50%;top:14px;bottom:14px;width:4px;background:var(--an-border);transform:translateX(-50%);border-radius:2px;cursor:pointer;"></div>
                                            <div id="acpTcvSliderThumb" style="position:absolute;left:50%;width:16px;height:16px;background:#00c8ff;border:2px solid #e8f4ff;border-radius:50%;transform:translate(-50%,-50%);cursor:grab;top:14px;box-shadow:0 0 4px rgba(0,0,0,.6);"></div>
                                            <div id="acpTcvSliderTopLbl" style="position:absolute;top:1px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);font-size:8px;color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080);white-space:nowrap;">0 m</div>
                                            <div id="acpTcvSliderBotLbl" style="position:absolute;bottom:1px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);font-size:8px;color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080);white-space:nowrap;">TD</div>
                                            <div id="acpTcvSliderVal" style="position:absolute;left:48px;font-size:10px;color:var(--an-text-bright,#e8f4ff);font-family:monospace;white-space:nowrap;background:var(--an-panel,#111820);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid var(--an-border);top:14px;pointer-events:none;">0 m</div>
                                        </div>
                                        <div style="flex:1;min-width:0;background:var(--an-panel2,#161e28);border:1px solid var(--an-border);border-radius:4px;padding:8px;position:relative;">
                                            <canvas id="acpChartTCV"></canvas>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div style="font-size:10px;color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080);margin-top:8px;">
                                        Standard Traveling Cylinder Plot construction (Thorogood &amp; Sawaryn, SPE 19989,
                                        1991): swept along the <b>reference well's own MD</b> (Reference MD ± Window above,
                                        step = MD Interval), building a fresh High Side/Right frame (High Side = "up",
                                        away from gravity; Right = hole azimuth + 90° — the view looking ahead, toward the
                                        bit) at <b>each</b> reference station. At each swept reference MD, every offset
                                        well's crossing of that station's normal plane (perpendicular to the reference
                                        well's tangent there) is found and plotted — the closest such crossing if a well
                                        crosses more than once. The reference well itself always sits exactly at the
                                        origin by construction and isn't plotted. Numbers along each trace are the
                                        <b>reference well's own MD</b> (m) at that crossing, not the offset well's MD. Uses
                                        <b>TVDss (Sub-Sea)</b> for the vertical component, same as the C2C/SF charts above.
                                        A well with no crossing in the swept window (e.g. it stays entirely ahead or
                                        behind every plane in range, or every crossing falls outside Max Scan Radius)
                                        simply has no trace. Radius rings auto-scale to the data, capped at Max Scan
                                        Radius. Depth labels default off (Show Depths to enable — with many offset wells
                                        the numbers overlap heavily). Scroll to zoom in/out; the reference well stays
                                        fixed at the plot's center at every zoom level (this plot is inherently about
                                        distance FROM that center, so panning off it isn't offered). Use the reset
                                        button above to return to the auto-fit view.
                                    </div>
                                </div>

                                <div style="font-size:10px;color:var(--an-text-dim,#5a7080);margin-top:8px;">
                                    <b>Left — C2C:</b> center-to-center distance from the reference well to the closest point
                                    on each other wellbore's 3D trajectory, at every survey station along the reference well —
                                    same closest-approach method as the Frac Planes / AC Scan tool. Uses Northing/Easting
                                    and <b>TVDss (Sub-Sea)</b>, not raw TVD — TVD is referenced to each well's own RKB/KB
                                    elevation, which can differ between wells, so it isn't safe to compare directly across
                                    wells; Sub-Sea is a common datum and is correct for this. Default view is 0–20 m;
                                    scroll/pinch to zoom, drag to pan, or use Reset Zoom. Click any point on either chart to
                                    inspect the raw N/E/TVDss of both matched stations.<br>
                                    <b>Right — SF:</b> the <b>reference well</b> uses its own saved <b>Toolcode</b> (editable
                                    via the dropdown above, persisted per wellbore). <b>Offset wells</b> are temporarily all
                                    assumed to use <code>MWD+HRGM</code> — there's no per-offset-well toolcode picker yet
                                    (planned as a pad-level control); until then this is a simplification, not each well's
                                    real tool. Both use the real ISCWSA MWD Rev5 error model (validated against ISCWSA's own
                                    test-well data — see <code>iscwsaModel.js</code>) and each well's Total Field/Dip/
                                    Declination from the magnetics cards above. Falls back to a simplified approximate model
                                    automatically for any well missing survey inc/azim or magnetics data. Gyro toolcodes
                                    aren't implemented yet (MWD only). Default view is 0–2 (SF is a dimensionless ratio; the
                                    decision-relevant range is near 1) — zoom/pan to see further; values are capped at 20 for
                                    display (very shallow depths, near-zero uncertainty, would otherwise compute as
                                    infinite). Global-term correlation between wells uses the base ISCWSA propagation-mode
                                    rule (fully correlated, not the fractional refinement from ISCWSA's separate
                                    geomagnetic-correlation supplement).
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

